A||||3||contra||performance improvements for the 2.8L?||||4||
Z||000000||contra||09-30-2000||09:52 AM||||I'm currently having a great time with my 87GT, but i wouldnt mind more kick out of it. I am seriously thinking about adding a NOS system, but what other upgrades could i do for under $1000 each?<P><BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||88formula||09-30-2000||12:56 PM||||You can get an underdrive pulley from he Fiero Store, $80 and 6 HP gain. MSD ignition coil from Summit racing, $35 and 1-2 peak HP gain. You can get FOCOA headers from FOCOA, $600 and about 12-15 peak HP and better gas mileage. An aluminum flywheel from Fieroshop $550 and about 8-10 HP gain throughout the RPM band. You can port your exhaust manifolds for about $50 in labor and supplies and gain about 8-10 peak HP and better gas mileage. You can add a bigger cam and gain 8-15 peak HP. You can port your heads and gain another 5-10 peak HP. You can get a performance muffler or exhaust and gain 2-5 HP. <P>Keep in mind that these figures are not cumulative but are just a guess of what you would gain form a stock 2.8 with that one modification alone and no other. Most of these modifications will cause you to loose something in return for the gain. For example the exhaust work, cam, ported heads, will give you more upper peak horsepower but you may loose low end horsepower and torque. The Aluminum flywheel and underdrive pulley on the other hand will cause you to loose nothing because all they do is reduce the parasitic drag on the motor freeing up the horsepower that you would otherwise loose to the parasitic drag. The coil only increases your combustion efficiency by elimination and misfires at upper Rpm’s.<P>Did I miss anything?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||09-30-2000||02:47 PM||||Not trying to start anything here, but y'know, everytime I hear about underdrive pulleys, I can't help but think (ouch! that hurts!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )...<P>1. It can't be any fun swapping out pulleys (and belts?). Sound like actual <B>work</B> - something I usually try to avoid.  So you do this work, and you get some more go, but in everyday traffic, you risk undercharging, overheating, reduced A/C capacity, etc. <P>2. You can cut out the A/C compressor electrically (in fact, the ECM does it for you anyway).<P>3. It's quite possible to cut out the drag from the alternator electrically (for the duration of a drag race or "spurt of go," or whatever).<P>That leaves the water pump - which I think I would sooner leave alone.  On non-Fieros with power steering, you could devise a little clutch (similar to the one on the A/C compressor), or a solenoid-operated "bypass" valve to relieve the load on the PS pump.    <BR> <BR>The bottom line is, you should be able to make a system where you can have your cake and eat it, too.  I bet I'd be happier with an "on-demand-only" accessory drive cutout. You could flip a switch, and go from "stock" mode (full time accessories), to "on-demand" mode (cuts out accessories when you stomp it), to "race?" mode (cuts out accessories immediately).  <P>Again, not trying to argue or anything.  Just venting an idea, for what it's worth  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  ||||reg||3
Z||000003||contra||09-30-2000||03:33 PM||||yeah i know what you mean about the A/C etc<BR>i remember seeing a show on honda and import racing and those guys had the coolest ECM's. They would hookup laptops to their ECM and turn on and off dipswitches for different devices. They could turn off their A/C and richen their fuel, and just about everything else. i was pretty jealous actually<BR>hehehe<BR>||||reg||1
